#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719937 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "The magnitude uses both coordinate derivatives: $\\sqrt{1+(2t)^2}$, not just $2t$." :answer/id #uuid "0e6346d1-2dd8-5416-8cfa-b03d9dac9c3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{1}2t^3\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719920} {:answer/feedback "The arc-length factor uses the derivative $2t$, not the coordinate $t^2$." :answer/id #uuid "442748b5-a70c-5d0c-afa6-1975be7bba13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{1}t^2\\sqrt{1+t^4}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719927} {:answer/feedback "Here $y=t^2$ and $\\mathrm{d}s=\\sqrt{1+4t^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t$." :answer/id #uuid "698de1ac-8a85-569c-8cbd-937222158e0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{1}t^2\\sqrt{1+4t^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719932} {:answer/feedback "Include the arc-length factor $\\|\\mathbf r\\,\\!{}^{\\prime}(t)\\|=\\sqrt{1+4t^2}$." :answer/id #uuid "b490bcfe-9282-5bb5-b2f2-f1db9140e9da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{1}t^2\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719935} {:answer/feedback "The scalar function is $y=t^2$, not $x=t$." :answer/id #uuid "c6357767-9d9b-5092-9ee9-72ab8faca86b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{1}t\\sqrt{1+4t^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719938}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/feedback "Here $y=t^2$ and $\\mathrm{d}s=\\sqrt{1+4t^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t$." :answer/id #uuid "698de1ac-8a85-569c-8cbd-937222158e0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{1}t^2\\sqrt{1+4t^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719932} :answer-field/id #uuid "ae8fffbb-b2e6-5920-b2b6-3d64902358f7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186719934}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bfd51ac0-2555-51de-8834-1bc176a6746d" :question/problem "The curve $C$ is the section of $y=x^2$ for $0\\le x\\le 1$, shown below.\n\n![The parabola from (0,0) to (1,1).](images/a8/a8a3fe6c05479258f84aa074398e92a8a849fa4d015feb450aeef6a6066a870e.png)\n\nWhich definite integral is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\int_C y\\,\\mathrm{d}s\n$$\n\nusing $x=t$? Do not evaluate the integral." :question/worked-solution "Set $x=t$ and $y=t^2$. The parameter interval is $0\\le t\\le 1$, so\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=\\langle t,t^2\\rangle.\n$$\n\nDifferentiate both coordinates and take the magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf r'(t)&=\\langle 1,2t\\rangle,\\\\\n\\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{1^2+(2t)^2}=\\sqrt{1+4t^2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe scalar function is $f(x,y)=y$, hence $f(\\mathbf r(t))=t^2$. Combining this with the arc-length factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int_C y\\,\\mathrm{d}s\n&=\\int_0^1 f(\\mathbf r(t))\\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\\\\n&=\\int_0^1 t^2\\sqrt{1+4t^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186720008 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "991123ae-1303-5008-b3e2-6441a2d4f7f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720019}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "991123ae-1303-5008-b3e2-6441a2d4f7f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720019} :answer-field/id #uuid "428f479f-b774-56a2-af34-3c7b7abc35df" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720013}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "15ddf2ef-6e79-5f49-aada-6eb336e74ad7" :question/problem "Given $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle-2,0,0\\rangle$, $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle-2,-1,3\\rangle$, $\\mathbf{c}=\\langle1,1,1\\rangle$, find $\\mathbf{a}\\cdot(\\mathbf{b}\\times\\mathbf{c})$ using the definition of the scalar triple product.\n\n$\\mathbf{a}\\cdot(\\mathbf{b}\\times\\mathbf{c})=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, compute the ordered cross product $\\mathbf{b}\\times\\mathbf{c}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{b}\\times\\mathbf{c}&=\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf{i}&\\mathbf{j}&\\mathbf{k}\\\\-2&-1&3\\\\1&1&1\\end{vmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIts components are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nd_1&=(-1)\\cdot1-3\\cdot1=-4 \\\\\nd_2&=-((-2)\\cdot1-3\\cdot1)=5 \\\\\nd_3&=(-2)\\cdot1-(-1)\\cdot1=-1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus $\\mathbf{b}\\times\\mathbf{c}=\\langle-4,5,-1\\rangle$. Now take the dot product with $\\mathbf{a}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{a}\\cdot(\\mathbf{b}\\times\\mathbf{c})&=\\langle-2,0,0\\rangle\\cdot\\langle-4,5,-1\\rangle \\\\\n&=(-2)\\cdot(-4)+0\\cdot5+0\\cdot(-1) \\\\\n&=8+0+0 \\\\\n&=8\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186720011 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6398832c-feb0-588b-98b8-e256e7d65258" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720017}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6398832c-feb0-588b-98b8-e256e7d65258" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720017} :answer-field/id #uuid "b656037c-a48a-5bf6-9932-eac1bc57165c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720021}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "31d75d9e-4bf3-5af9-9659-2709bc1a3222" :question/problem "Given $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle-1,3,-2\\rangle$, $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle1,0,2\\rangle$, $\\mathbf{c}=\\langle2,-3,-2\\rangle$, find $\\mathbf{a}\\cdot(\\mathbf{b}\\times\\mathbf{c})$ using the definition of the scalar triple product.\n\n$\\mathbf{a}\\cdot(\\mathbf{b}\\times\\mathbf{c})=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, compute the ordered cross product $\\mathbf{b}\\times\\mathbf{c}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{b}\\times\\mathbf{c}&=\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf{i}&\\mathbf{j}&\\mathbf{k}\\\\1&0&2\\\\2&-3&-2\\end{vmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIts components are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nd_1&=0\\cdot(-2)-2\\cdot(-3)=6 \\\\\nd_2&=-(1\\cdot(-2)-2\\cdot2)=6 \\\\\nd_3&=1\\cdot(-3)-0\\cdot2=-3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus $\\mathbf{b}\\times\\mathbf{c}=\\langle6,6,-3\\rangle$. Now take the dot product with $\\mathbf{a}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{a}\\cdot(\\mathbf{b}\\times\\mathbf{c})&=\\langle-1,3,-2\\rangle\\cdot\\langle6,6,-3\\rangle \\\\\n&=(-1)\\cdot6+3\\cdot6+(-2)\\cdot(-3) \\\\\n&=(-6)+18+6 \\\\\n&=18\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186720018 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1cacae63-c2d6-561d-99ff-23e49584e3e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720009} {:answer/id #uuid "38b9ec19-6316-5e4e-b7a9-83960c43e5c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720012} {:answer/id #uuid "51df7b9e-1436-5e16-a329-403672f50875" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720015} {:answer/id #uuid "b983de20-123f-55f8-91f9-42f329aea062" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720023} {:answer/id #uuid "d561a6f1-73c6-58e4-bd16-14958da2b4d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720026}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "51df7b9e-1436-5e16-a329-403672f50875" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720015} :answer-field/id #uuid "eb1282aa-89e3-56a4-b620-f9b2c5979d80" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720028}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8fb0dbf3-6caa-538e-8b86-936971956f01" :question/problem "Given $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle2,1,-3\\rangle$, $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle-2,-2,-2\\rangle$, $\\mathbf{c}=\\langle0,3,0\\rangle$, find $\\mathbf{a}\\cdot(\\mathbf{b}\\times\\mathbf{c})$ using the definition of the scalar triple product." :question/worked-solution "First, compute the ordered cross product $\\mathbf{b}\\times\\mathbf{c}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{b}\\times\\mathbf{c}&=\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf{i}&\\mathbf{j}&\\mathbf{k}\\\\-2&-2&-2\\\\0&3&0\\end{vmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIts components are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nd_1&=(-2)\\cdot0-(-2)\\cdot3=6 \\\\\nd_2&=-((-2)\\cdot0-(-2)\\cdot0)=0 \\\\\nd_3&=(-2)\\cdot3-(-2)\\cdot0=-6\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus $\\mathbf{b}\\times\\mathbf{c}=\\langle6,0,-6\\rangle$. Now take the dot product with $\\mathbf{a}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{a}\\cdot(\\mathbf{b}\\times\\mathbf{c})&=\\langle2,1,-3\\rangle\\cdot\\langle6,0,-6\\rangle \\\\\n&=2\\cdot6+1\\cdot0+(-3)\\cdot(-6) \\\\\n&=12+0+18 \\\\\n&=30\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186720022 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29d8bdee-5598-5552-a8a6-91b6fa4e23d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720010} {:answer/id #uuid "506080b1-0ace-5115-8161-2691d9a83f5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720014} {:answer/id #uuid "5ff06e3a-2e8b-57cd-a04e-4fd3b56846ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "69" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720016} {:answer/id #uuid "cb13fd32-9878-54b4-ab0a-ab03bbf303f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "33" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720024} {:answer/id #uuid "cbdb9088-5c7b-5848-9a72-37280fc439a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720025}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cb13fd32-9878-54b4-ab0a-ab03bbf303f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "33" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720024} :answer-field/id #uuid "a7e72508-81af-5f17-bf15-8b7ad330eb4d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720020}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b6fabfb3-cbc1-5226-b779-69314ec40ae9" :question/problem "Given $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle3,3,2\\rangle$, $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle3,-1,3\\rangle$, $\\mathbf{c}=\\langle0,-3,-2\\rangle$, find $\\mathbf{a}\\cdot(\\mathbf{b}\\times\\mathbf{c})$ using the definition of the scalar triple product." :question/worked-solution "First, compute the ordered cross product $\\mathbf{b}\\times\\mathbf{c}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{b}\\times\\mathbf{c}&=\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf{i}&\\mathbf{j}&\\mathbf{k}\\\\3&-1&3\\\\0&-3&-2\\end{vmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIts components are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nd_1&=(-1)\\cdot(-2)-3\\cdot(-3)=11 \\\\\nd_2&=-(3\\cdot(-2)-3\\cdot0)=6 \\\\\nd_3&=3\\cdot(-3)-(-1)\\cdot0=-9\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus $\\mathbf{b}\\times\\mathbf{c}=\\langle11,6,-9\\rangle$. Now take the dot product with $\\mathbf{a}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{a}\\cdot(\\mathbf{b}\\times\\mathbf{c})&=\\langle3,3,2\\rangle\\cdot\\langle11,6,-9\\rangle \\\\\n&=3\\cdot11+3\\cdot6+2\\cdot(-9) \\\\\n&=33+18+(-18) \\\\\n&=33\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186720029 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "edd8d5a2-6014-5ac2-972e-7f9dacc2ac66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720030}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "edd8d5a2-6014-5ac2-972e-7f9dacc2ac66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720030} :answer-field/id #uuid "d68cd8f3-90c8-545c-8b22-716a4e7bd6b3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720027}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "eb818d3d-a8e1-55db-bfd3-bbd106e36032" :question/problem "Given $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle1,-1,1\\rangle$, $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle-2,2,-3\\rangle$, $\\mathbf{c}=\\langle1,-3,2\\rangle$, find $\\mathbf{a}\\cdot(\\mathbf{b}\\times\\mathbf{c})$ using the definition of the scalar triple product.\n\n$\\mathbf{a}\\cdot(\\mathbf{b}\\times\\mathbf{c})=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, compute the ordered cross product $\\mathbf{b}\\times\\mathbf{c}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{b}\\times\\mathbf{c}&=\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf{i}&\\mathbf{j}&\\mathbf{k}\\\\-2&2&-3\\\\1&-3&2\\end{vmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIts components are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nd_1&=2\\cdot2-(-3)\\cdot(-3)=-5 \\\\\nd_2&=-((-2)\\cdot2-(-3)\\cdot1)=1 \\\\\nd_3&=(-2)\\cdot(-3)-2\\cdot1=4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus $\\mathbf{b}\\times\\mathbf{c}=\\langle-5,1,4\\rangle$. Now take the dot product with $\\mathbf{a}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{a}\\cdot(\\mathbf{b}\\times\\mathbf{c})&=\\langle1,-1,1\\rangle\\cdot\\langle-5,1,4\\rangle \\\\\n&=1\\cdot(-5)+(-1)\\cdot1+1\\cdot4 \\\\\n&=(-5)+(-1)+4 \\\\\n&=-2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186720034 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "50564360-a7f8-52b3-8ddf-b165916240c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720036} {:answer/id #uuid "542b33fd-1a98-53a2-8922-2eca070cf886" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720037} {:answer/id #uuid "5a3ec8f5-b676-566e-862d-49365d9e0339" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720038} {:answer/id #uuid "99408149-2ec3-5c09-bf62-78d7f7a0f3c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720042} {:answer/id #uuid "d2e906a2-2ae5-575b-abfb-3298529ef9f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720045}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "99408149-2ec3-5c09-bf62-78d7f7a0f3c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720042} :answer-field/id #uuid "2c1875a4-11a2-5af3-b2f7-4dc941e19c52" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720032}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2fd242c8-b740-51bc-8675-871df76fe608" :question/problem "Let $\\mathbf a=\\langle0,2,1\\rangle$, $\\mathbf b=\\langle1,0,2\\rangle$, and $\\mathbf c=\\langle2,1,3\\rangle$. Find $\\mathbf a\\cdot(\\mathbf b\\times\\mathbf c)$ using a determinant. Use $\\mathbf a$, $\\mathbf b$, and $\\mathbf c$, in that order, as its rows." :question/worked-solution "The rows follow the order in $\\mathbf a\\cdot(\\mathbf b\\times\\mathbf c)$: $\\mathbf a$, $\\mathbf b$, $\\mathbf c$. The scalar triple product equals the determinant of these rows.\n\n$$\n\\mathbf a\\cdot(\\mathbf b\\times\\mathbf c)=\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 3\\end{vmatrix}\n$$\n\nCall this determinant $D$. Expand across the first row using the cofactor signs $+,-,+$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D&=0\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{vmatrix}-2\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{vmatrix}+1\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ &=0-2(1\\cdot3-2\\cdot2)+(1\\cdot1-0\\cdot2) \\\\ &=0+2+1 \\\\ &=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186720035 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f6a85cdc-ad34-5360-a624-40218b4145dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "34" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720048}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f6a85cdc-ad34-5360-a624-40218b4145dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "34" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720048} :answer-field/id #uuid "8ece2000-5941-5354-bc87-2eedba3dd624" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720041}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "483fdc09-1d78-5dc4-810a-794a2161a6fa" :question/problem "Let $\\mathbf p=\\langle1,-2,2\\rangle$, $\\mathbf q=\\langle-2,1,3\\rangle$, and $\\mathbf r=\\langle2,3,-1\\rangle$. Find $\\mathbf r\\cdot(\\mathbf q\\times\\mathbf p)$ using a determinant.\n\n$\\mathbf r\\cdot(\\mathbf q\\times\\mathbf p)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The rows follow the order in $\\mathbf r\\cdot(\\mathbf q\\times\\mathbf p)$: $\\mathbf r$, $\\mathbf q$, $\\mathbf p$. The scalar triple product equals the determinant of these rows.\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r\\cdot(\\mathbf q\\times\\mathbf p)=\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 3 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 2\\end{vmatrix}\n$$\n\nCall this determinant $D$. Expand across the first row using the cofactor signs $+,-,+$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D&=2\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{vmatrix}-3\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{vmatrix}+(-1)\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ &=2(1\\cdot2-3(-2)) \\\\ &\\quad -3((-2)\\cdot2-3\\cdot1) \\\\ &\\quad +(-1)((-2)(-2)-1\\cdot1) \\\\ &=16+21-3 \\\\ &=34.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186720040 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6363ab9b-c805-534f-87e0-832711ea615e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720039} {:answer/id #uuid "b4ee300f-5f85-55fa-b2e0-ab655ea12e07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720043} {:answer/id #uuid "b76cc9f9-aa78-5935-96a2-68037d8d9c2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720044} {:answer/id #uuid "e5709eed-aece-55a4-b24c-e256433f89cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720046} {:answer/id #uuid "ec6250f9-c1bd-551f-a101-8eb01dbc7729" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720047}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ec6250f9-c1bd-551f-a101-8eb01dbc7729" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720047} :answer-field/id #uuid "2f011fbe-d07c-529f-8009-83159e544c22" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720033}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "779664ac-9c51-5a56-8d80-fbf493afcadc" :question/problem "Let $\\mathbf p=\\langle1,2,1\\rangle$, $\\mathbf q=\\langle2,-1,0\\rangle$, and $\\mathbf r=\\langle-1,1,2\\rangle$. Find $\\mathbf q\\cdot(\\mathbf p\\times\\mathbf r)$ using a determinant." :question/worked-solution "The rows follow the order in $\\mathbf q\\cdot(\\mathbf p\\times\\mathbf r)$: $\\mathbf q$, $\\mathbf p$, $\\mathbf r$. The scalar triple product equals the determinant of these rows.\n\n$$\n\\mathbf q\\cdot(\\mathbf p\\times\\mathbf r)=\\begin{vmatrix}2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 2\\end{vmatrix}\n$$\n\nCall this determinant $D$. Expand across the first row using the cofactor signs $+,-,+$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D&=2\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{vmatrix}-(-1)\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{vmatrix}+0\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ &=2(2\\cdot2-1\\cdot1)-(-1)(1\\cdot2-1(-1))+0 \\\\ &=6+3+0 \\\\ &=9.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186720055 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25468fb2-f320-5214-a36d-4e408f49f632" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720053}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "25468fb2-f320-5214-a36d-4e408f49f632" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720053} :answer-field/id #uuid "7de2c167-006c-5332-82b8-c06315cefb16" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720056}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "53e00711-3582-58bd-9f40-4dc5abc9be30" :question/problem "Suppose\n\n$$\n(2\\mathbf{b})\\times(-\\mathbf{c})=\\langle4,-6,2\\rangle,\n\\qquad \\mathbf{a}=\\langle1,2,-1\\rangle.\n$$\n\nFind $(2\\mathbf{b})\\cdot\\bigl((3\\mathbf{a})\\times(-\\mathbf{c})\\bigr)$.\n\n$(2\\mathbf{b})\\cdot\\bigl((3\\mathbf{a})\\times(-\\mathbf{c})\\bigr)=$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Use the supplied cross product; no individual coordinates for $\\mathbf{b}$ or $\\mathbf{c}$ are needed. First take its dot product with $\\mathbf{a}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{a}\\cdot\\bigl((2\\mathbf{b})\\times(-\\mathbf{c})\\bigr)\n&=\\langle1,2,-1\\rangle\\cdot\\langle4,-6,2\\rangle\\\\\n&=1(4)+2(-6)+(-1)(2)\\\\\n&=-10.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $T=\\mathbf{a}\\cdot(\\mathbf{b}\\times\\mathbf{c})$. Factoring out the two scalars gives\n\n$$\n-2T=-10,\\qquad T=5.\n$$\n\nSwapping $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ changes the sign:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{b}\\cdot(\\mathbf{a}\\times\\mathbf{c})=-T=-5.\n$$\n\nNow factor the scalars out of the requested product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(2\\mathbf{b})\\cdot\\bigl((3\\mathbf{a})\\times(-\\mathbf{c})\\bigr)\n&=2(3)(-1)\\bigl[\\mathbf{b}\\cdot(\\mathbf{a}\\times\\mathbf{c})\\bigr]\\\\\n&=(-6)(-5)\\\\\n&=30.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquivalently, swap $\\mathbf{a}$ and $2\\mathbf{b}$ in the computed product $-10$, then multiply the new outer vector $\\mathbf{a}$ by $3$: $-3(-10)=30$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186720057 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "94e24455-6144-5bb3-96fe-def255486a6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720059}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "94e24455-6144-5bb3-96fe-def255486a6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720059} :answer-field/id #uuid "0f2aab28-b9f5-5ac2-acaa-1dc4e66784ef" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720050}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "83675788-ac10-5c6d-86e5-befa99486885" :question/problem "Find $\\mathbf{c}\\cdot(\\mathbf{a}\\times\\mathbf{b})$, given\n\n$$\n(2\\mathbf{a})\\cdot\\bigl((-3\\mathbf{b})\\times\\mathbf{c}\\bigr)=9.\n$$\n\n$\\mathbf{c}\\cdot(\\mathbf{a}\\times\\mathbf{b})=$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First factor out the scalars:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(2\\mathbf{a})\\cdot\\bigl((-3\\mathbf{b})\\times\\mathbf{c}\\bigr)\n&=2(-3)\\bigl[\\mathbf{a}\\cdot(\\mathbf{b}\\times\\mathbf{c})\\bigr]=9,\\\\\n\\mathbf{a}\\cdot(\\mathbf{b}\\times\\mathbf{c})&=-\\frac{3}{2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSwap $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{c}$, then swap $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$. Each swap changes the sign:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c}\\cdot(\\mathbf{b}\\times\\mathbf{a})&=\\frac{3}{2},\\\\\n\\mathbf{c}\\cdot(\\mathbf{a}\\times\\mathbf{b})&=-\\frac{3}{2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe two sign changes cancel, so the requested product is $-\\frac{3}{2}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186720058 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a818287-7df0-5aed-b1fa-c168130d16f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720049} {:answer/id #uuid "1ad9010a-353e-5812-a75e-b9a48fcc15bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720051} {:answer/id #uuid "209421f2-a3d1-5bb9-8822-d2bc275eb92d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720052} {:answer/id #uuid "9a27ef3f-6a44-5caf-98a9-6a38ebf44afd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720060} {:answer/id #uuid "ce043f41-b77d-5d2a-a4bd-5f2f5f9d3305" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720061}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ce043f41-b77d-5d2a-a4bd-5f2f5f9d3305" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720061} :answer-field/id #uuid "4063a538-8c19-5590-8042-bde096327aaa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720054}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8a925dc8-06d9-5d64-b262-31d44c94bf71" :question/problem "Given $\\mathbf{a}\\cdot(\\mathbf{b}\\times\\mathbf{c})=-6$, find $\\mathbf{b}\\cdot(\\mathbf{a}\\times\\mathbf{c})$." :question/worked-solution "Swapping exactly two vectors in a scalar triple product changes its sign. Swap $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{b}\\cdot(\\mathbf{a}\\times\\mathbf{c})\n&=-\\mathbf{a}\\cdot(\\mathbf{b}\\times\\mathbf{c})\\\\\n&=-(-6)\\\\\n&=6.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186720143 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "000adedb-7b5a-5ce6-8c2a-93d9fb8ac188" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720139} {:answer/id #uuid "05cafa44-dc42-5d11-b832-62852b17d3b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720140} {:answer/id #uuid "c882783e-69be-513a-85d9-b4d83bd374a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 2 \\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720164} {:answer/id #uuid "d008fe87-abf6-5e1a-9fc6-a41b12f06a9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720167} {:answer/id #uuid "d6e46a71-14c8-5ac8-923a-6fdb84aa6d83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720169}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "05cafa44-dc42-5d11-b832-62852b17d3b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720140} :answer-field/id #uuid "731b4c4b-c2d5-544a-b292-dad06a4a995b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720153}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3d8c4c53-1406-52d6-a728-523f521adca0" :question/problem "Evaluate the scalar line integral\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\left(- \\frac{1}{x - y}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}s\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is given by $y=x - 1$ for $-2\\le x\\le -1$." :question/worked-solution "Set $x=t$ and use the explicit equation to parametrize the curve:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=\\langle t,t - 1\\rangle,\\qquad -2\\le t\\le -1\n$$\n\nDifferentiate and calculate the nonnegative speed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf r'(t)&=\\langle1,1\\rangle\\\\\n\\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{1+\\left(1\\right)^2}=\\sqrt{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute both coordinates into the scalar function:\n\n$$\nf(\\mathbf r(t))=f\\left(t,t - 1\\right)=-1\n$$\n\nInclude the speed factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int_C f\\,\\mathrm{d}s&=\\int_{-2}^{-1} f(\\mathbf r(t))\\|\\mathbf r\\prime(t)\\|\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\\\\n&=\\int_{-2}^{-1}\\left(-1\\right)\\left(\\sqrt{2}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplify the product before integrating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int_C f\\,\\mathrm{d}s&=\\int_{-2}^{-1}\\left(- \\sqrt{2}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\\\\n&=\\left[- \\sqrt{2} t\\right]_{-2}^{-1}\\\\\n&=\\left(\\sqrt{2}\\right)-\\left(2 \\sqrt{2}\\right)\\\\\n&=- \\sqrt{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186720147 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "795084fc-a056-522f-8b2b-23dd8000c8a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720154} {:answer/id #uuid "8ae0e639-2e31-574b-983b-efd2ffb65d59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3 \\sqrt{5}}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720156} {:answer/id #uuid "9bea7bc9-551a-50ed-8d33-c9d6a03285d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9 \\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720159} {:answer/id #uuid "b47231a6-9673-5440-bbe2-9ac16cfd4c62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3 \\sqrt{5}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720162} {:answer/id #uuid "cfe4d052-ac1e-53e7-bd77-cd294e97917e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3 \\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720166}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b47231a6-9673-5440-bbe2-9ac16cfd4c62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3 \\sqrt{5}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720162} :answer-field/id #uuid "9daf4ec2-8d67-5c32-8418-37338f22bfb5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720160}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5cddf83d-53a7-5b22-8d88-c1f63f9402c7" :question/problem "Evaluate the scalar line integral\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\left(x + y\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}s\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is given by $y=2 x - 1$ for $-1\\le x\\le 2$." :question/worked-solution "Set $x=t$ and use the explicit equation to parametrize the curve:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=\\langle t,2 t - 1\\rangle,\\qquad -1\\le t\\le 2\n$$\n\nDifferentiate and calculate the nonnegative speed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf r'(t)&=\\langle1,2\\rangle\\\\\n\\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{1+\\left(2\\right)^2}=\\sqrt{5}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute both coordinates into the scalar function:\n\n$$\nf(\\mathbf r(t))=f\\left(t,2 t - 1\\right)=3 t - 1\n$$\n\nInclude the speed factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int_C f\\,\\mathrm{d}s&=\\int_{-1}^{2} f(\\mathbf r(t))\\|\\mathbf r\\prime(t)\\|\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\\\\n&=\\int_{-1}^{2}\\left(3 t - 1\\right)\\left(\\sqrt{5}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplify the product before integrating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int_C f\\,\\mathrm{d}s&=\\int_{-1}^{2}\\left(\\sqrt{5} \\left(3 t - 1\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\\\\n&=\\left[\\sqrt{5} \\left(\\frac{3 t^{2}}{2} - t\\right)\\right]_{-1}^{2}\\\\\n&=\\left(4 \\sqrt{5}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{5 \\sqrt{5}}{2}\\right)\\\\\n&=\\frac{3 \\sqrt{5}}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186720151 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ded20b9-ea7e-596f-9553-606623be1ca4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{9 \\sqrt{10}}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720141} {:answer/id #uuid "377a9318-6fca-5138-8aa5-3e991e553d4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 8 \\sqrt{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720142} {:answer/id #uuid "6c607306-df70-5b93-a33f-76813ff9ebe1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 9 \\sqrt{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720150} {:answer/id #uuid "d1e3d220-9cf8-5f06-a273-784654b73f97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 6 \\sqrt{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720168} {:answer/id #uuid "ea9bf2e5-5b59-5062-aeb9-a7c9ede8b2a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 7 \\sqrt{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720171}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6c607306-df70-5b93-a33f-76813ff9ebe1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 9 \\sqrt{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720150} :answer-field/id #uuid "e81dc837-ba8b-5e7a-86d3-86dd535d2ca7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720170}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "70436e97-25d7-5963-8bc0-2ef6378a4137" :question/problem "Evaluate the scalar line integral\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\left(- x \\left(y + 2\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}s\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is given by $y=3 x - 2$ for $-1\\le x\\le 2$." :question/worked-solution "Set $x=t$ and use the explicit equation to parametrize the curve:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=\\langle t,3 t - 2\\rangle,\\qquad -1\\le t\\le 2\n$$\n\nDifferentiate and calculate the nonnegative speed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf r'(t)&=\\langle1,3\\rangle\\\\\n\\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{1+\\left(3\\right)^2}=\\sqrt{10}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute both coordinates into the scalar function:\n\n$$\nf(\\mathbf r(t))=f\\left(t,3 t - 2\\right)=- 3 t^{2}\n$$\n\nInclude the speed factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int_C f\\,\\mathrm{d}s&=\\int_{-1}^{2} f(\\mathbf r(t))\\|\\mathbf r\\prime(t)\\|\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\\\\n&=\\int_{-1}^{2}\\left(- 3 t^{2}\\right)\\left(\\sqrt{10}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplify the product before integrating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int_C f\\,\\mathrm{d}s&=\\int_{-1}^{2}\\left(- 3 \\sqrt{10} t^{2}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\\\\n&=\\left[- \\sqrt{10} t^{3}\\right]_{-1}^{2}\\\\\n&=\\left(- 8 \\sqrt{10}\\right)-\\left(\\sqrt{10}\\right)\\\\\n&=- 9 \\sqrt{10}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186720163 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4cbecc2d-af2b-548a-8d9c-b8f3a4e11452" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{40}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720145} {:answer/id #uuid "62b05fdd-0be6-5f52-9d97-ae6f9145c9d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{20}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720149} {:answer/id #uuid "725f974e-89da-5bbf-9785-593815f79da1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{16 \\sqrt{5}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720152} {:answer/id #uuid "79ede7a4-0093-5ad4-97c7-6b115a8e4ab8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{20 \\sqrt{5}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720155} {:answer/id #uuid "cad9c227-48cb-5622-b3cd-26f27edbaee4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{100}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720165}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "79ede7a4-0093-5ad4-97c7-6b115a8e4ab8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{20 \\sqrt{5}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720155} :answer-field/id #uuid "58074c07-95df-5e61-a168-255bf4ca3b01" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720146}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c5681a32-e6dc-54c8-969c-49b11b3f81e6" :question/problem "Evaluate the scalar line integral\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\left(2 x^{2} + 2 y\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}s\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is given by $y=- 2 x - 1$ for $0\\le x\\le 2$." :question/worked-solution "Set $x=t$ and use the explicit equation to parametrize the curve:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=\\langle t,- 2 t - 1\\rangle,\\qquad 0\\le t\\le 2\n$$\n\nDifferentiate and calculate the nonnegative speed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf r'(t)&=\\langle1,-2\\rangle\\\\\n\\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{1+\\left(-2\\right)^2}=\\sqrt{5}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute both coordinates into the scalar function:\n\n$$\nf(\\mathbf r(t))=f\\left(t,- 2 t - 1\\right)=2 t^{2} - 4 t - 2\n$$\n\nInclude the speed factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int_C f\\,\\mathrm{d}s&=\\int_{0}^{2} f(\\mathbf r(t))\\|\\mathbf r\\prime(t)\\|\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\\\\n&=\\int_{0}^{2}\\left(2 t^{2} - 4 t - 2\\right)\\left(\\sqrt{5}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplify the product before integrating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int_C f\\,\\mathrm{d}s&=\\int_{0}^{2}\\left(2 \\sqrt{5} \\left(t^{2} - 2 t - 1\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\\\\n&=\\left[\\sqrt{5} \\left(\\frac{2 t^{3}}{3} - 2 t^{2} - 2 t\\right)\\right]_{0}^{2}\\\\\n&=\\left(- \\frac{20 \\sqrt{5}}{3}\\right)-\\left(0\\right)\\\\\n&=- \\frac{20 \\sqrt{5}}{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186720173 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c057246-5739-5438-9f09-fddec50c0b04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720144} {:answer/id #uuid "608d721d-b091-5dd9-b311-2f2dc92c9f47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720148} {:answer/id #uuid "96f6b856-a4ba-54f1-b38f-dedf10c01f7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720158} {:answer/id #uuid "a7278935-55ad-58ad-8bec-3b46f7f944df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720161} {:answer/id #uuid "f38114df-adbc-5430-9246-24eda4e01eb8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720172}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "96f6b856-a4ba-54f1-b38f-dedf10c01f7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720158} :answer-field/id #uuid "8e88fc81-a54a-5647-b7c3-3f40c6fb68e4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720157}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fab8da42-c5fb-5d1a-8792-fca8e6298fe5" :question/problem "Evaluate the scalar line integral\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\left(\\frac{1}{x - y}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}s\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is given by $y=x + 2$ for $-1\\le x\\le 1$." :question/worked-solution "Set $x=t$ and use the explicit equation to parametrize the curve:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=\\langle t,t + 2\\rangle,\\qquad -1\\le t\\le 1\n$$\n\nDifferentiate and calculate the nonnegative speed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf r'(t)&=\\langle1,1\\rangle\\\\\n\\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{1+\\left(1\\right)^2}=\\sqrt{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute both coordinates into the scalar function:\n\n$$\nf(\\mathbf r(t))=f\\left(t,t + 2\\right)=- \\frac{1}{2}\n$$\n\nInclude the speed factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int_C f\\,\\mathrm{d}s&=\\int_{-1}^{1} f(\\mathbf r(t))\\|\\mathbf r\\prime(t)\\|\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\\\\n&=\\int_{-1}^{1}\\left(- \\frac{1}{2}\\right)\\left(\\sqrt{2}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplify the product before integrating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int_C f\\,\\mathrm{d}s&=\\int_{-1}^{1}\\left(- \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\\\\n&=\\left[- \\frac{\\sqrt{2} t}{2}\\right]_{-1}^{1}\\\\\n&=\\left(- \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)\\\\\n&=- \\sqrt{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186720179 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "174cdcc4-9b16-5904-aefa-38dbed9954d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186720177} {:answer/id #uuid "2a49c00f-367e-58ab-9f82-18c999b57d27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :an